            <ArticleTitle>Finally, an APC code for observation: now find out the rules for getting paid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51; suppl 1 p.</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new ambulatory payment classification code was created for observation, with a payment rate of $351. Three diagnoses qualify for reimbursement: congestive heart failure, chest pain, and asthma. Active physician involvement in assessment and writing orders is required. Nurses should document the time when physician orders were started.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
